.TH SLIPFORK 1 "2026-11-21" "slipfork 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slipfork \- copy-on-write Btrfs worlds for polyglot apps and coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slipfork
.RI [ verb ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slipfork
reads a
.I Forkfile
in the current directory and runs its images, databases, caches, buckets, and
workers on native Btrfs subvolumes and
.BR crun ,
behind one
.I .localhost
domain.
No Docker daemon is involved.
Every world starts through a single per-user daemon that the CLI starts on demand.
.SH VERBS
.TP
.B status
Show every running world as a tree.
Flags: \fB--json\fR, \fB-v\fR, \fB--verbose\fR.
.TP
.B ps
Show only the world or fork rooted in this directory.
Flags: \fB--json\fR, \fB-v\fR, \fB--verbose\fR.
.TP
.B doctor
Check Btrfs, namespaces, and the crun + \fB:80\fR runtime, and print
\fB\(check Ready\fR or \fB\(cross N issue(s)\fR first.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B up
Boot the world declared by \fI./Forkfile\fR and return when it is ready.
Flags: \fB--world\fR, \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B down
Stop the running world in this directory.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B restart
Restart one service, or every service.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B fork
Snapshot the project and world data, then boot the fork on its own URL.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B drop
Stop a fork and delete its project and world-data snapshots.
Flags: \fB-f\fR, \fB--force\fR, \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B logs
Stream merged stdout and stderr with per-service gutters.
Flags: \fB-f\fR, \fB--follow\fR, \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B shell
Open a shell inside a service or image pod.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B exec
Run a command inside a pod and forward its exit code.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B db
Open psql against the world postgres.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B redis
Open redis-cli against the world redis.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B env
Print resolved runtime variables; secrets stay redacted unless revealed.
Flags: \fB--reveal\fR, \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B secret
List, override, or remove local offline secrets.
Subcommands: \fBlist\fR, \fBset\fR, \fBunset\fR.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B open
Open the world or service URL in your browser, headless-aware.
Flags: \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B auth
Pair this machine with a remote OSPP v1 endpoint.
Flags: \fB--ospp-endpoint\fR, \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B fmt
Format a Forkfile in place.
Flags: \fB--check\fR, \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B migrate
Convert a legacy \fIsnow.yml\fR into a Forkfile.
Flags: \fB--write\fR, \fB--force\fR, \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B completions
Print a shell completion script for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, or \fBfish\fR.
.TP
.B daemon install
Write the per-user unit under \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/systemd/user\fR.
With \fB--ingress\fR and root, also install \fBslipfork-ingress.socket\fR,
\fBslipfork-ingress@.service\fR, and the AppArmor profile.
Flags: \fB--ingress\fR, \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B help
Print the overview.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./Forkfile
The world declaration read by \fBup\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/systemd/user/slipfork.service
The per-user daemon unit \fBdaemon install\fR writes.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/slipfork.service
The package's per-user unit copy; enable it with \fBsystemctl --user enable slipfork\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/slipfork-ingress.socket
The \fB127.0.0.1:80\fR socket unit the package ships.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/slipfork-ingress@.service
The per-connection handoff template; \fBdaemon install --ingress\fR rewrites its
\fBUser=\fR for the invoking developer.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/slipfork-ingress.socket
Where \fBdaemon install --ingress\fR writes the runtime socket unit.
.TP
.I /etc/apparmor.d/slipfork
The user-namespace profile the package ships.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable every ANSI escape; \fB--json\fR does the same for machine output.
.TP
.B SLIPFORK_WORLD
The world a shell or plugin command targets.
.TP
.B SLIPFORK_URL
The URL a fork or world is reachable at.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slipfork-lsp (1),
.BR crun (1),
.BR btrfs (8)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/OffworldNexus/slipfork/issues.
